From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 06n-arch <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:45:00 -0500
Subject: drm/panthor: don't block on a syncobj BO's resv under sched->lock

sync_upd_work() evaluates blocked queues with sched->lock held, and the
evaluation takes the synchronization object's BO reservation lock
uninterruptibly: drm_gem_vmap() on first use, panthor_gem_sync() for the
CPU cache invalidation (not a NOP here: 3001 makes Sky1 BOs write-back),
drm_gem_vunmap() once satisfied.

Private BOs share their VM's reservation lock, and the GEM shrinker can
hold it while waiting on the VM's fences: it trylocks a BO, waits up to
10 jiffies for its fences, moves to the next BO of the same VM, and so
on. Those fences can't signal while sync_upd_work() sits on sched->lock
waiting for that reservation, with tick_work, process_fw_events_work and
every GROUP_GET_STATE caller (Mesa, kwin_wayland) queued behind it. The
whole GPU stalls until memory pressure lets up.

Seen on a Radxa Orion O6N (Mali-G720, 32 GB): Deep Rock Galactic under
DXVK grew to 20 GB of GPU memory; hung-task reports showed sync_upd_work
in panthor_gem_sync() -> ww_mutex_lock, and everything else in
mutex_lock(&sched->lock). It only cleared once the game's processes were
killed and memory was freed.

Evaluate the sync wait under a single dma_resv_trylock(): map, invalidate,
read the seqno and unmap with the reservation held, and drop the BO
reference after unlocking. If the trylock fails, the queue stays blocked
and sync_upd_work() retries a jiffy later: sync updates are the only
thing that re-evaluates blocked queues, so a skipped queue needs an
explicit retry.

panthor_gem_sync() is split into panthor_gem_sync_locked() for this; the
vmap/vunmap hooks are called directly because drm_gem_vmap_locked() is
declared in drm_internal.h.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_gem.c   |  49 +++++---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_gem.h   |   2 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_sched.c | 160 ++++++++++++++++--------
 3 files changed, 139 insertions(+), 72 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_gem.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_gem.c
index f926b1fb1..516ee393a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_gem.c
@@ -1138,16 +1138,26 @@ panthor_gem_kernel_bo_set_label(struct panthor_kernel_bo *bo, const char *label)
 	panthor_gem_bo_set_label(bo->obj, str);
 }
 
+/**
+ * panthor_gem_sync_locked() - CPU cache maintenance on a BO range
+ * @obj: Object to sync.
+ * @type: DRM_PANTHOR_BO_SYNC_CPU_CACHE_* operation.
+ * @offset: Start of the range.
+ * @size: Size of the range.
+ *
+ * Same as panthor_gem_sync(), with the BO reservation lock already held.
+ *
+ * Return: 0 on success, a negative error code otherwise.
+ */
 int
-panthor_gem_sync(struct drm_gem_object *obj, u32 type,
-		 u64 offset, u64 size)
+panthor_gem_sync_locked(struct drm_gem_object *obj, u32 type,
+			u64 offset, u64 size)
 {
 	struct panthor_gem_object *bo = to_panthor_bo(obj);
 	struct device *dma_dev = drm_dev_dma_dev(bo->base.dev);
 	struct sg_table *sgt;
 	struct scatterlist *sgl;
 	unsigned int count;
-	int ret;
 
 	/* Make sure the range is in bounds. */
 	if (offset + size < offset || offset + size > bo->base.size)
@@ -1174,21 +1184,15 @@ panthor_gem_sync(struct drm_gem_object *obj, u32 type,
 	if (size == 0)
 		return 0;
 
-	ret = dma_resv_lock_interruptible(bo->base.resv, NULL);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+	dma_resv_assert_held(bo->base.resv);
 
 	/* If there's no pages, there's no point pulling those back, bail out early. */
-	if (!bo->backing.pages) {
-		ret = 0;
-		goto out_unlock;
-	}
+	if (!bo->backing.pages)
+		return 0;
 
 	sgt = panthor_gem_dev_map_get_sgt_locked(bo);
-	if (IS_ERR(sgt)) {
-		ret = PTR_ERR(sgt);
-		goto out_unlock;
-	}
+	if (IS_ERR(sgt))
+		return PTR_ERR(sgt);
 
 	for_each_sgtable_dma_sg(sgt, sgl, count) {
 		if (size == 0)
@@ -1232,10 +1236,21 @@ panthor_gem_sync(struct drm_gem_object *obj, u32 type,
 			dma_sync_single_for_cpu(dma_dev, paddr, len, DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
 	}
 
-	ret = 0;
+	return 0;
+}
 
-out_unlock:
-	dma_resv_unlock(bo->base.resv);
+int
+panthor_gem_sync(struct drm_gem_object *obj, u32 type,
+		 u64 offset, u64 size)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = dma_resv_lock_interruptible(obj->resv, NULL);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = panthor_gem_sync_locked(obj, type, offset, size);
+	dma_resv_unlock(obj->resv);
 	return ret;
 }
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_gem.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_gem.h
index 5ae37d0d3..1b2686c0b 100644
